    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54">

                <pb facs="0144" n="42" xml:id="pg42"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 General Committee (Arms)/209:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-04-03T19:00:00+00:00">April 3, 1935—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 3—3:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>158. With reference to recent French proposals at Geneva for amplifying notice of
                    laying down naval vessels envisaged in present clauses taken from Washington and
                    London treaties and included in American draft proposal convention covering
                    trade and manufacture of armament, Captain Danckwerts, in the presence of
                    Admiral Bellairs, expressed to Naval Attaché today attitude of British
                    Government as follows: British Government views French proposition
                    sympathetically but believes it should be held in abeyance until proposals
                    discussed last autumn in London naval negotiations<anchor n="64" xml:id="d54-f1"
                    /> for qualitative and quantitative limitation of naval vessels or,
                    alternatively, proposal for declared building programs be further discussed and
                    definitely accepted or rejected. These latter proposals to be considered if a
                    naval conference is called this year.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d54-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Naval Attaché requests copy of this telegram be transmitted for the information
                    of naval intelligence.</p>
                <p>Geneva informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
